  "title": "The Robot Who Collected Exceptions",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "fantasy and science fiction",
  "premise": "A tidy robot wants to sort every object into square or round boxes, but a teardrop-shaped keepsake fits neither rule. Instead of cutting it to fit, the robot adds an EXCEPTIONS shelf, then finds that the shelf holds the most interesting objects in the room and gives each a small name tag.",
  "hook": "This shape is not in my instructions.",
  "visible_action": "Robot rotates keepsake against two box openings; cutting icon is crossed out; new shelf extends; odd shapes gather with individual labels.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A useful system can make room for things outside its first categories.",
  "gate": "Fictional robot behavior; no assertion about actual AI capabilities, sentience, or classification fairness.",
  "evidence_class": "fictional_demonstration",
